{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": false,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [
    {
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "GIDEON"
      ],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "title": "GIDEON boards",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": false,
      "targetBlank": false
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "description": "This lists the page-class alerts firing now. An empty list means no page needs attention; a listed rule needs action. The Saturday heartbeat is not a page and never appears here. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "viewMode": "list",
        "groupMode": "default",
        "groupBy": [],
        "maxItems": 20,
        "sortOrder": 4,
        "dashboardAlerts": false,
        "alertName": "",
        "showInstances": true,
        "showInactiveAlerts": false,
        "alertInstanceLabelFilter": "{class=\"page\"}",
        "stateFilter": {
          "firing": true,
          "pending": false,
          "noData": true,
          "normal": false,
          "error": true,
          "recovering": false
        }
      },
      "title": "Needs attention",
      "type": "alertlist"
    },
    {
      "description": "This points to the box status command, Grafana's silences page, the boards available on this host, and the start-here card. A clear status report is good; a reported problem needs action. Begin with docs/runbooks/start-here.md §1.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "On the box, run `gideon status` for what needs attention now. Before planned work, [silence the rule that would page](/grafana/alerting/silences).\n\nThe other boards on this host:\n\n- [GIDEON Backup](/grafana/d/gideon-backup)\n\nThe start-here card: `/opt/gideon/docs/runbooks/start-here.md` on the box, or <a href=\"https://github.com/TNMD-FDO/GIDEON/blob/vfixture/docs/runbooks/start-here.md\" target=\"_blank\">in the public export at this release</a>."
      },
      "title": "Start here",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows one tile per check a down rule watches: a tile named for a service is its metrics scrape, a tile ending in probe is the door check itself, and a tile ending in database is the database check. Up is healthy; a tile down for ten minutes (five for the engine) causes a page. Each tile is named in docs/runbooks/observability.md §3. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "up",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "down",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 14,
          "valueSize": 28
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "up",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "probe_success",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{job}} probe",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "pg_up",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{job}} database",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Services and probes",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows the percentage of space free on /data, /, and /var/lib/docker, reported by the host monitor. At least 15 percent free is healthy; less than that causes a page. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 15
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "displayMode": "basic",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "showUnfilled": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "100 * node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint=\"/data\"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/data\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "/data",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "100 * node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "/",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "100 * node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint=\"/var/lib/docker\"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/var/lib/docker\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "/var/lib/docker",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Filesystems free",
      "type": "bargauge"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows whole days until the ingress certificate expires, from its probe. 14 days or more is healthy; fewer causes a page, and a renewal needs lead time from the office CA. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "suffix: days",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 14
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "floor((probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry{job=\"ingress\"} - time()) / 86400)",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "certificate",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Certificate days left",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows time since the newest completed backup set, from its recorded run. Under 26 hours is good; an older or missing set causes a page. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gideon-rows"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 93600
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (now() - max(at))) AS age_seconds FROM audit_log WHERE kind = 'backup_run' AND detail->>'phase' = 'applied'",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Backup set age",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows time since the newest off-box backup copy, from its recorded push. Under 26 hours is good; an older or missing push causes a page. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gideon-rows"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 93600
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 16
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (now() - max(at))) AS age_seconds FROM audit_log WHERE kind = 'backup_push'",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Backup push age",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows time since the newest passing backup drill, from its recorded result. Under 38 days is good; an older or missing passing drill causes a page. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gideon-rows"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3283200
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (now() - max(at))) AS age_seconds FROM audit_log WHERE kind = 'backup_drill' AND detail->>'result' = 'pass'",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Passing drill age",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This shows the newest recorded backup drill result. Pass means the restore checks succeeded; failed means they did not and causes a page. Follow docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gideon-rows"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "pass": {
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "failed": {
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 16
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "/^result$/",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT at AS time, detail->>'result' AS result FROM audit_log WHERE kind = 'backup_drill' ORDER BY at DESC LIMIT 1",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Last drill result",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "description": "This charts daily counts of user questions caught by each guardrail rule, from recorded trips. Some trips are expected; a sudden rise can mean more questions are being refused. Review docs/runbooks/guardrail.md §3.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gideon-rows"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars"
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "format": "time_series",
          "rawSql": "SELECT date_trunc('day', at) AS time, pattern_id AS metric, count(*) AS trips FROM guardrail_trips WHERE source = 'user' AND $__timeFilter(at) GROUP BY date_trunc('day', at), pattern_id ORDER BY time",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "timeFrom": "30d",
      "title": "Guardrail trips",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "description": "This shows the host's average work waiting or running over one minute, reported by the host monitor. A steady value is normal; sustained growth can mean the box is overloaded. Check docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "short"
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 6,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 31
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "list",
              "placement": "bottom"
            }
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "node_load1",
              "legendFormat": "load 1m",
              "refId": "A"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Host load",
          "type": "timeseries"
        },
        {
          "description": "This shows the percentage of host memory in use, calculated from the host monitor's available and total memory. A stable value with room left is good; a value near full leaves little room for work. Check docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percent"
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 6,
            "x": 6,
            "y": 31
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "list",
              "placement": "bottom"
            }
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "100 * (1 - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)",
              "legendFormat": "memory used",
              "refId": "A"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Host memory",
          "type": "timeseries"
        },
        {
          "description": "This compares each service container's memory in use with its configured limit, from the container monitor. Use below the limit is normal; use near the limit leaves little room and may interrupt service. Check docs/runbooks/observability.md §4.",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "bytes"
            },
            "overrides": [
              {
                "matcher": {
                  "id": "byRegexp",
                  "options": "/ limit$/"
                },
                "properties": [
                  {
                    "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                    "value": {
                      "fill": "dash",
                      "dash": [
                        10,
                        10
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 12,
            "y": 31
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom"
            }
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "sum by (name) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{name!=\"\"})",
              "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
              "refId": "A"
            },
            {
              "expr": "sum by (name) (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name!=\"\"} > 0)",
              "legendFormat": "{{name}} limit",
              "refId": "B"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Container memory",
          "type": "timeseries"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Host detail",
      "type": "row"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "tags": [
    "GIDEON",
    "overview"
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "timezone": "browser",
  "title": "GIDEON Overview",
  "uid": "gideon-overview",
  "version": 1
}
